e preserving animation and scene references.","Base reuse on the CC0 designation of the downloaded files. A free edition does not establish entitlement to paid source files or unrelated marketplace content.",[1113,1114],{"_42":1116,"_24":1117},{"_42":1115,"_24":694},"Example pack and edition details","Creator asset catalog and licensing","https://quaternius.com/",[1119],{"_42":240,"_24":1117},"CC0 for creator-designated asset packs; check each download",[1122],{"_42":1123,"_24":1117,"_259":1124},"Browse creator packs","Check the exact pack: free Standard downloads and paid Pro or Source editions can contain different files.",[1126],{"_42":261,"_24":1117},"Low-poly environments, characters and animated model packs",[272],[141,73],[143,77],[289],{"_42":1123,"_24":1117,"_259":1124},[1136,1137],[1109,1110],[1106,1107],{"_42":1116,"_24":1117},{"_42":1115,"_24":694},"testing:kenney","kenney","Kenney","A practical CC0 starting point for small test scenes, asset replacement, collision and UI regressions.","/testing/kenney/",{"_18":1139,"_20":1140,"_16":827,"_275":1187,"_271":1188,"_268":1184,"_278":1141,"_263":1180,"_256":1189,"_253":252,"_250":1176,"_246":408,"_242":749,"_233":1190,"_230":1170,"_225":1191,"_219":1192,"_213":1163,"_210":209},[1145,1146,1147,1148,1149,1150,1151,1152,1153,1154,1155,1156,1157,1158,1159,1160,1161,1162],{"_40":20,"_44":1140,"_46":20,"_48":-7},{"_40":70,"_44":1141,"_46":278,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":276,"_44":826,"_46":16,"_48":75},{"_40":214,"_42":273,"_216":223,"_52":1186,"_46":275,"_48":-7},{"_40":214,"_42":269,"_216":223,"_52":1185,"_46":271,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":266,"_44":1184,"_46":268,"_48":49},{"_40":50,"_42":261,"_52":1182,"_46":263,"_48":-7},{"_40":50,"_42":254,"_52":1177,"_46":256,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":251,"_44":252,"_46":253,"_48":49},{"_40":41,"_42":248,"_44":1176,"_46":250,"_48":49},{"_40":41,"_42":244,"_44":394,"_46":246,"_48":247},{"_40":50,"_42":240,"_52":1174,"_46":242,"_48":-7},{"_40":50,"_42":231,"_52":1171,"_46":233,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":228,"_44":1170,"_46":230,"_48":49},{"_40":214,"_42":222,"_216":223,"_52":1167,"_46":225,"_48":-7},{"_40":214,"_42":215,"_216":217,"_52":1164,"_46":219,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":211,"_44":1163,"_46":213,"_48":49},{"_40":41,"_42":208,"_44":209,"_46":210,"_48":75},"Not every pack contains animation or a humanoid rig. No pack was imported locally in this review.",[1165,1166],"Choose one small pack and retain its included license file.","Import the pack into a versioned test project and record the import settings.",[1168,1169],"Replace a sprite or model and check scale, collision and material references.","Run a fixed UI or tilemap scene and compare screenshots.","Use the CC0 pack files as the basis for a redistributable test fixture. This does not make the website, branding or separately sold software CC0.",[1172],{"_42":1173,"_24":749},"Creator licensing FAQ",[1175],{"_42":240,"_24":749},"CC0 for the asset packs",[1178],{"_42":1179,"_24":1180,"_259":1181},"Browse free asset packs","https://kenney.nl/assets","Individual asset packs are free; optional bundles and tools are separate products.",[1183],{"_42":261,"_24":1180},"Sprites, tiles, UI, audio and 3D model packs",[824,272],[141,73],[143,77],[836,289],{"_42":1179,"_24":1180,"_259":1181},[1193],[1168,1169],[1165,1166],{"_42":1173,"_24":749},"testing:unity-ml-agents","unity-ml-agents","Unity ML-Agents","An official toolkit and example scenes for physics, visual control, cooperation and competition. It can expose custom Unity scenes to Python policies and automated tests.","/testing/unity-ml-agents/",{"_18":1195,"_20":1196,"_16":1260,"_275":1261,"_271":1262,"_268":1256,"_278":1197,"_263":1255,"_256":1263,"_253":1247,"_250":1246,"_246":1264,"_242":1244,"_233":1265,"_230":1228,"_225":1266,"_219":1267,"_213":1219,"_210":209},[1201,1202,1203,1204,1205,1206,1207,1208,1209,1210,1211,1212,1213,1214,1215,1216,1217,1218],{"_40":20,"_44":1196,"_46":20,"_48":-7},{"_40":70,"_44":1197,"_46":278,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":276,"_44":1259,"_46":16,"_48":75},{"_40":214,"_42":273,"_216":223,"_52":1258,"_46":275,"_48":-7},{"_40":214,"_42":269,"_216":223,"_52":1257,"_46":271,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":266,"_44":1256,"_46":268,"_48":49},{"_40":50,"_42":261,"_52":1253,"_46":263,"_48":-7},{"_40":50,"_42":254,"_52":1248,"_46":256,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":251,"_44":1247,"_46":253,"_48":49},{"_40":41,"_42":248,"_44":1246,"_46":250,"_48":49},{"_40":41,"_42":244,"_44":1245,"_46":246,"_48":247},{"_40":50,"_42":240,"_52":1242,"_46":242,"_48":-7},{"_40":50,"_42":231,"_52":1229,"_46":233,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":228,"_44":1228,"_46":230,"_48":49},{"_40":214,"_42":222,"_216":223,"_52":1224,"_46":225,"_48":-7},{"_40":214,"_42":215,"_216":217,"_52":1220,"_46":219,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":211,"_44":1219,"_46":213,"_48":49},{"_40":41,"_42":208,"_44":209,"_46":210,"_48":75},"Source reviewed, not run here. Editor eligibility, platform builds and version compatibility need local checks. The develop branch is not a stable evaluation baseline.",[1221,1222,1223],"Select a release tag, install its supported Unity editor and open the included Project.","Install the matching com.unity.ml-agents package and Python environment package versions.","Open an example scene and connect a policy; route actions by behavior and agent_id, and read both DecisionSteps and TerminalSteps. Python step advances to the next decision, not necessarily one physics frame.",[1225,1226,1227],"Compare physics-task success with fixed observations, decisions and reset rules.","Change a C# agent or scene and verify sensors, rewards and episode termination.","Import a replacement rig or collider and check control stability and visual observations.","The toolkit supports agent research and automated testing; its Apache license does not replace editor or third-party asset terms.",[1230,1231,1232,1233],{"_42":1240,"_24":1241},{"_42":1238,"_24":1239},{"_42":1236,"_24":1237},{"_42":1234,"_24":1235},"Unity editor terms","https://unity.com/legal/editor-terms-of-service/software","Third-party notices","https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/ml-agents/blob/develop/Third%20Party%20Notices.md","Release 23 low-level decision and terminal contract","https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/ml-agents/blob/a2777719560e4676be99e2ea128c5eb1fbeb3dbb/com.unity.ml-agents/Documentation~/Python-LLAPI.md","Official toolkit and release compatibility","https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/ml-agents#readme",[1243],{"_42":240,"_24":1244},"https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/ml-agents/blob/develop/LICENSE.md","Engine-specific terms","Check bundled notices and any added scene assets. The Unity editor and external store assets have separate terms.","Apache-2.0 for the toolkit, with third-party notices.",[1249],{"_42":1250,"_24":1251,"_259":1252},"Free toolkit; Unity editor required","https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/ml-agents/releases","Choose one release and match its Unity package, Python packages and supported editor version.",[1254],{"_42":261,"_24":1255},"https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/ml-agents","Unity · C# · Python · sensors and agent actions",[824,272],[141,108,73],"AI evaluation environments","environment",[143,110,77],[836,289],{"_42":1250,"_24":1251,"_259":1252},"engine",[1268,1269,1270,1271],[1225,1226,1227],[1221,1222,1223],{"_42":1240,"_24":1241},{"_42":1238,"_24":1239},{"_42":1236,"_24":1237},{"_42":1234,"_24":1235},"testing:godot-rl-agents","godot-rl-agents","Godot RL Agents","Connects editable Godot games to Python agents. Useful for changing gameplay, exposing observations and evaluating NPC control in a scene you own.","/testing/godot-rl-agents/",{"_18":1273,"_20":1274,"_16":1260,"_275":1332,"_271":1333,"_268":1329,"_278":1275,"_263":1328,"_256":1334,"_253":1321,"_250":1320,"_246":952,"_242":1319,"_233":1335,"_230":1306,"_225":1336,"_219":1337,"_213":1297,"_210":209},[1279,1280,1281,1282,1283,1284,1285,1286,1287,1288,1289,1290,1291,1292,1293,1294,1295,1296],{"_40":20,"_44":1274,"_46":20,"_48":-7},{"_40":70,"_44":1275,"_46":278,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":276,"_44":1259,"_46":16,"_48":75},{"_40":214,"_42":273,"_216":223,"_52":1331,"_46":275,"_48":-7},{"_40":214,"_42":269,"_216":223,"_52":1330,"_46":271,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":266,"_44":1329,"_46":268,"_48":49},{"_40":50,"_42":261,"_52":1326,"_46":263,"_48":-7},{"_40":50,"_42":254,"_52":1322,"_46":256,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":251,"_44":1321,"_46":253,"_48":49},{"_40":41,"_42":248,"_44":1320,"_46":250,"_48":49},{"_40":41,"_42":244,"_44":937,"_46":246,"_48":247},{"_40":50,"_42":240,"_52":1317,"_46":242,"_48":-7},{"_40":50,"_42":231,"_52":1307,"_46":233,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":228,"_44":1306,"_46":230,"_48":49},{"_40":214,"_42":222,"_216":223,"_52":1302,"_46":225,"_48":-7},{"_40":214,"_42":215,"_216":217,"_52":1298,"_46":219,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":211,"_44":1297,"_46":213,"_48":49},{"_40":41,"_42":208,"_44":209,"_46":210,"_48":75},"Source reviewed, not run here. The inspected bridge sends env_seed when launching a binary, but reset(seed=...) sends only a reset message. Editor runs need scene/plugin seed control; validate reset repeatability rather than assuming the Python argument reseeds Godot.",[1299,1300,1301],"Install godot-rl in a Python environment and download a documented example such as JumperHard.","Use the matching Godot 4 .NET editor for the documented editor example; import the project.","Run the repository Stable Baselines 3 example, or adapt its environment interface to a fixed policy.",[1303,1304,1305],"Change movement or reward logic, establish reset/replay repeatability for that scene, then compare fixed input rollouts.","Test sensors, action scaling and Python-to-game synchronization.","Replace a character or collider and verify that observations and control still work.","Designed for learning and automated gameplay testing. Keep imported-model rights and example attributions alongside the MIT toolkit license.",[1308,1309,1310],{"_42":1315,"_24":1316},{"_42":1313,"_24":1314},{"_42":1311,"_24":1312},"Pinned binary-launch and reset seed behavior","https://github.com/edbeeching/godot_rl_agents/blob/207b6f476f5846f33d08b92c7a350147e7b78bf5/godot_rl/core/godot_env.py","Example asset attribution","https://github.com/edbeeching/godot_rl_agents#license","Editor and exported-game workflow","https://github.com/edbeeching/godot_rl_agents#quickstart-guide",[1318],{"_42":240,"_24":1319},"https://github.com/edbeeching/godot_rl_agents/blob/main/LICENSE","Example assets can have separate notices: the Cartoon Plane model is CC BY 4.0.","MIT for Godot RL Agents; Godot is also MIT.",[1323],{"_42":1324,"_24":1316,"_259":1325},"Free toolkit and example projects","Install godot-rl and import an example; editor operation avoids needing a prebuilt game binary.",[1327],{"_42":261,"_24":1328},"https://github.com/edbeeching/godot_rl_agents","Godot 4 · Python · game sensors and action bridge",[824,272],[141,108,73],[143,110,77],[836,289],{"_42":1324,"_24":1316,"_259":1325},[1338,1339,1340],[1303,1304,1305],[1299,1300,1301],{"_42":1315,"_24":1316},{"_42":1313,"_24":1314},{"_42":1311,"_24":1312},"testing:nethack-learning-environment","nethack-learning-environment","NetHack Learning Environment","A demanding roguelike interface for exploration, inventory, tactical choices and long-term planning. Use the maintained NetHack-LE organization rather than the archived Facebook repository.","/testing/nethack-learning-environment/",{"_18":1342,"_20":1343,"_16":1260,"_275":1402,"_271":1403,"_268":1399,"_278":1344,"_263":1398,"_256":1404,"_253":1390,"_250":1389,"_246":408,"_242":1388,"_233":1405,"_230":1375,"_225":1406,"_219":1407,"_213":1366,"_210":209},[1348,1349,1350,1351,1352,1353,1354,1355,1356,1357,1358,1359,1360,1361,1362,1363,1364,1365],{"_40":20,"_44":1343,"_46":20,"_48":-7},{"_40":70,"_44":1344,"_46":278,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":276,"_44":1259,"_46":16,"_48":75},{"_40":214,"_42":273,"_216":223,"_52":1401,"_46":275,"_48":-7},{"_40":214,"_42":269,"_216":223,"_52":1400,"_46":271,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":266,"_44":1399,"_46":268,"_48":49},{"_40":50,"_42":261,"_52":1396,"_46":263,"_48":-7},{"_40":50,"_42":254,"_52":1391,"_46":256,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":251,"_44":1390,"_46":253,"_48":49},{"_40":41,"_42":248,"_44":1389,"_46":250,"_48":49},{"_40":41,"_42":244,"_44":394,"_46":246,"_48":247},{"_40":50,"_42":240,"_52":1386,"_46":242,"_48":-7},{"_40":50,"_42":231,"_52":1376,"_46":233,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":228,"_44":1375,"_46":230,"_48":49},{"_40":214,"_42":222,"_216":223,"_52":1371,"_46":225,"_48":-7},{"_40":214,"_42":215,"_216":217,"_52":1367,"_46":219,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":211,"_44":1366,"_46":213,"_48":49},{"_40":41,"_42":208,"_44":209,"_46":210,"_48":75},"Source reviewed, not run here. Native tools may be required. In the inspected code, reset(seed=...) seeds Gymnasium but does not set NetHack RNGs; use the explicit seed interface. NetHackChallenge deliberately disallows seed changes. Terminal/glyph observations are not RGB game frames.",[1368,1369,1370],"Prepare Python 3.10+, CMake 3.28+ and the platform build prerequisites documented upstream.","Install nle, then run python -m nle.scripts.play --mode random.","Create NetHackScore-v0 with fixed observation_keys, actions and fix_moon_phase=True; before reset, call env.unwrapped.seed with recorded core, disp, reseed=False and optional lgen values.",[1372,1373,1374],"Measure staircase or score-task progress with a fixed turn budget.","Test inventory decisions and recovery after invalid actions.","Modify a task reward or termination rule and replay baseline rollouts.","An AI research interface; distinguish terminal rendering, symbols, text messages and internal state so planning results remain comparable.",[1377,1378,1379],{"_42":1384,"_24":1385},{"_42":1382,"_24":1383},{"_42":1380,"_24":1381},"Pinned observation, seed and reset implementation","https://github.com/NetHack-LE/nle/blob/2319f2989f0035685017e9ea13c83b2546fe477c/nle/env/base.py","Archived upstream repository","https://github.com/facebookresearch/nle","Maintained source, installation and play scripts","https://github.com/NetHack-LE/nle#readme",[1387],{"_42":240,"_24":1388},"https://github.com/NetHack-LE/nle/blob/main/LICENSE","Bundled NetHack data follows repository notices; external tilesets are separate.","NetHack General Public License; preserve notices and follow source/distribution obligations.",[1392],{"_42":1393,"_24":1394,"_259":1395},"Free package and source","https://github.com/NetHack-LE/nle#installation","Native compilation prerequisites may be needed; the repository includes interactive and random-agent scripts.",[1397],{"_42":261,"_24":1398},"https://github.com/NetHack-LE/nle","Python · C / C++ · Gymnasium · NetHack",[824],[141,108],[143,110],[836],{"_42":1393,"_24":1394,"_259":1395},[1408,1409,1410],[1372,1373,1374],[1368,1369,1370],{"_42":1384,"_24":1385},{"_42":1382,"_24":1383},{"_42":1380,"_24":1381},"testing:vizdoom","First-person environments for aiming, navigation, combat and memory, with programmable actions and scenario controls. The perspective is 3D; the renderer uses Doom-style technology.",{"_18":113,"_20":100,"_16":1260,"_275":1469,"_271":1470,"_268":1466,"_278":1412,"_263":1465,"_256":1471,"_253":1457,"_250":1456,"_246":952,"_242":1455,"_233":1472,"_230":1442,"_225":1473,"_219":1474,"_213":1433,"_210":209},[1415,1416,1417,1418,1419,1420,1421,1422,1423,1424,1425,1426,1427,1428,1429,1430,1431,1432],{"_40":20,"_44":100,"_46":20,"_48":-7},{"_40":70,"_44":1412,"_46":278,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":276,"_44":1259,"_46":16,"_48":75},{"_40":214,"_42":273,"_216":223,"_52":1468,"_46":275,"_48":-7},{"_40":214,"_42":269,"_216":223,"_52":1467,"_46":271,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":266,"_44":1466,"_46":268,"_48":49},{"_40":50,"_42":261,"_52":1463,"_46":263,"_48":-7},{"_40":50,"_42":254,"_52":1458,"_46":256,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":251,"_44":1457,"_46":253,"_48":49},{"_40":41,"_42":248,"_44":1456,"_46":250,"_48":49},{"_40":41,"_42":244,"_44":937,"_46":246,"_48":247},{"_40":50,"_42":240,"_52":1453,"_46":242,"_48":-7},{"_40":50,"_42":231,"_52":1443,"_46":233,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":228,"_44":1442,"_46":230,"_48":49},{"_40":214,"_42":222,"_216":223,"_52":1438,"_46":225,"_48":-7},{"_40":214,"_42":215,"_216":217,"_52":1434,"_46":219,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":211,"_44":1433,"_46":213,"_48":49},{"_40":41,"_42":208,"_44":209,"_46":210,"_48":75},"Source reviewed, not run here. ViZDoom 1.3+ macOS wheels require Apple Silicon and macOS 14+; the documented Intel wheel route is 1.2.4. Wrapper timeout handling changed in 1.3.0, so pin the version and timeout option. WAD rights remain scenario-specific.",[1435,1436,1437],"Install vizdoom in a supported Python environment; check wheel support for your OS and architecture.","Start from the repository Python examples and a bundled basic scenario.","For the Gymnasium wrapper, fix config, buffers, button space and frame_skip; use reset(seed=...) and log terminated and truncated separately, including treat_episode_timeout_as_truncation.",[1439,1440,1441],"Evaluate aiming accuracy, navigation completion and survival at a fixed action frequency.","Compare pixel-only control with privileged buffers explicitly marked as separate tracks.","Edit a scenario and check spawn, objectives, rewards and termination.","Built for AI experiments; this does not grant rights to arbitrary WADs. Record which scenario, base assets and licenses an evaluation uses.",[1444,1445,1446],{"_42":1451,"_24":1452},{"_42":1449,"_24":1450},{"_42":1447,"_24":1448},"Pinned Gymnasium timing, seed and timeout contract","https://github.com/Farama-Foundation/ViZDoom/blob/909e834264e42f136f59f80e72e95d8146f40e21/gymnasium_wrapper/base_gymnasium_env.py","Freedoom, WADs and custom scenarios","https://vizdoom.farama.org/faq/","Package installation and examples","https://github.com/Farama-Foundation/ViZDoom#python-quick-start",[1454],{"_42":240,"_24":1455},"https://github.com/Farama-Foundation/ViZDoom#license","Freedoom is the default asset set. Original Doom / Doom II WADs are not supplied and require their own rights.","Original ViZDoom contributions are MIT; underlying ZDoom components have separate licenses.",[1459],{"_42":1460,"_24":1461,"_259":1462},"Free package with Freedoom assets","https://vizdoom.farama.org/","pip install vizdoom; begin with a bundled scenario rather than a commercial Doom WAD.",[1464],{"_42":261,"_24":1465},"https://github.com/Farama-Foundation/ViZDoom","Python / C++ · Doom / ZDoom · Gymnasium",[272],[141,108],[143,110],[289],{"_42":1460,"_24":1461,"_259":1462},[1475,1476,1477],[1439,1440,1441],[1435,1436,1437],{"_42":1451,"_24":1452},{"_42":1449,"_24":1450},{"_42":1447,"_24":1448},"testing:craftax","craftax","Craftax","A survival and crafting environment with vectorized simulation. Useful for longer action dependencies and comparing pixel-based versus symbolic policies.","/testing/craftax/",{"_18":1479,"_20":1480,"_16":1260,"_275":1538,"_271":1539,"_268":1535,"_278":1481,"_263":1534,"_256":1540,"_253":1527,"_250":1526,"_246":408,"_242":1525,"_233":1541,"_230":1512,"_225":1542,"_219":1543,"_213":1503,"_210":209},[1485,1486,1487,1488,1489,1490,1491,1492,1493,1494,1495,1496,1497,1498,1499,1500,1501,1502],{"_40":20,"_44":1480,"_46":20,"_48":-7},{"_40":70,"_44":1481,"_46":278,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":276,"_44":1259,"_46":16,"_48":75},{"_40":214,"_42":273,"_216":223,"_52":1537,"_46":275,"_48":-7},{"_40":214,"_42":269,"_216":223,"_52":1536,"_46":271,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":266,"_44":1535,"_46":268,"_48":49},{"_40":50,"_42":261,"_52":1532,"_46":263,"_48":-7},{"_40":50,"_42":254,"_52":1528,"_46":256,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":251,"_44":1527,"_46":253,"_48":49},{"_40":41,"_42":248,"_44":1526,"_46":250,"_48":49},{"_40":41,"_42":244,"_44":394,"_46":246,"_48":247},{"_40":50,"_42":240,"_52":1523,"_46":242,"_48":-7},{"_40":50,"_42":231,"_52":1513,"_46":233,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":228,"_44":1512,"_46":230,"_48":49},{"_40":214,"_42":222,"_216":223,"_52":1508,"_46":225,"_48":-7},{"_40":214,"_42":215,"_216":217,"_52":1504,"_46":219,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":211,"_44":1503,"_46":213,"_48":49},{"_40":41,"_42":208,"_44":209,"_46":210,"_48":75},"Source reviewed, not run here. JIT startup is slow. With auto_reset=True, a done step returns the next episode observation/state alongside the previous episode reward/done/info. With auto_reset=False, handle termination before stepping again.",[1505,1506,1507],"Run pip install craftax in an isolated Python environment.","Run play_craftax or play_craftax_classic for manual play.","Select Craftax-Pixels-v1 or Craftax-Symbolic-v1 explicitly; keep full Craftax and Craftax-Classic separate. Supply distinct JAX keys to reset and step, and record the auto_reset setting.",[1509,1510,1511],"Compare survival and crafting progress using identical seeded worlds.","Separate image-only policies from symbolic-state policies.","Modify a block or recipe, invalidate texture caches when necessary, and check reset behavior.","Fix observation mode, PRNG keys, episode handling and package version. Version changes affect comparability: 1.5.0 fixes first-planted-plant growth, and 1.6.0 fixes Craftax-Classic death rewards.",[1514,1515,1516],{"_42":1521,"_24":1522},{"_42":1519,"_24":1520},{"_42":1517,"_24":1518},"Pinned auto-reset transition implementation","https://github.com/MichaelTMatthews/Craftax/blob/c3c2e0d038c4e641f9481320c158f457f30c28f3/craftax/environment_base/environment_bases.py","Game tutorial","https://github.com/MichaelTMatthews/Craftax/blob/main/tutorial.md","Installation, API and reset caveats","https://github.com/MichaelTMatthews/Craftax#readme",[1524],{"_42":240,"_24":1525},"https://github.com/MichaelTMatthews/Craftax/blob/main/LICENSE","Repository material under its MIT notice; added assets need separate records.","MIT.",[1529],{"_42":1530,"_24":1522,"_259":1531},"Free Python package","CPU JAX is installed by default; accelerator support needs the correct JAX build.",[1533],{"_42":261,"_24":1534},"https://github.com/MichaelTMatthews/Craftax","Python · JAX · gymnax-style API",[824],[141,108],[143,110],[836],{"_42":1530,"_24":1522,"_259":1531},[1544,1545,1546],[1509,1510,1511],[1505,1506,1507],{"_42":1521,"_24":1522},{"_42":1519,"_24":1520},{"_42":1517,"_24":1518},"testing:crafter","A compact survival world combining exploration, health, gathering, construction and crafting. Achievement progress exposes different strengths of a playing agent.",{"_18":112,"_20":102,"_16":1260,"_275":1607,"_271":1608,"_268":1604,"_278":1548,"_263":1603,"_256":1609,"_253":1527,"_250":1595,"_246":408,"_242":1594,"_233":1610,"_230":1578,"_225":1611,"_219":1612,"_213":1569,"_210":209},[1551,1552,1553,1554,1555,1556,1557,1558,1559,1560,1561,1562,1563,1564,1565,1566,1567,1568],{"_40":20,"_44":102,"_46":20,"_48":-7},{"_40":70,"_44":1548,"_46":278,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":276,"_44":1259,"_46":16,"_48":75},{"_40":214,"_42":273,"_216":223,"_52":1606,"_46":275,"_48":-7},{"_40":214,"_42":269,"_216":223,"_52":1605,"_46":271,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":266,"_44":1604,"_46":268,"_48":49},{"_40":50,"_42":261,"_52":1601,"_46":263,"_48":-7},{"_40":50,"_42":254,"_52":1596,"_46":256,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":251,"_44":1527,"_46":253,"_48":49},{"_40":41,"_42":248,"_44":1595,"_46":250,"_48":49},{"_40":41,"_42":244,"_44":394,"_46":246,"_48":247},{"_40":50,"_42":240,"_52":1592,"_46":242,"_48":-7},{"_40":50,"_42":231,"_52":1579,"_46":233,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":228,"_44":1578,"_46":230,"_48":49},{"_40":214,"_42":222,"_216":223,"_52":1574,"_46":225,"_48":-7},{"_40":214,"_42":215,"_216":217,"_52":1570,"_46":219,"_48":-7},{"_40":41,"_42":211,"_44":1569,"_46":213,"_48":49},{"_40":41,"_42":208,"_44":209,"_46":210,"_48":75},"Source reviewed, not run here. Classic Gym reset returns only an observation and step returns four values. reset has no seed argument; matching constructor seeds alone is insufficient unless episode/reset order also matches.",[1571,1572,1573],"Install crafter and pygame in an isolated Python environment.","Run python -m crafter.run_gui for manual controls, then use CrafterReward-v1 for automation.","Set the seed when constructing the environment and record the episode index; use crafter.Recorder with a nonempty output directory, save_stats=True and save_episode=True to retain completed-episode statistics and action trajectories.",[1575,1576,1577],"Measure survival and achievement success over held-out world seeds.","Plan a resource-to-tool sequence with a fixed interaction budget.","Change a recipe and verify that collection, crafting and achievement recording remain consistent.","Designed for agent evaluation. For pixel-only tests, withhold info.semantic, inventory and player_pos from the policy; those expose structured state beyond the RGB observation. Keep published benchmark budgets separate from custom VLM protocols.",[1580,1581,1582,1583],{"_42":1590,"_24":1591},{"_42":1588,"_24":1589},{"_42":1586,"_24":1587},{"_42":1584,"_24":1585},"Pinned completed-episode recorder contract","https://github.com/danijar/crafter/blob/e04542a2159f1aad3d4c5ad52e8185717380ee3a/crafter/recorder.py","Pinned reset, seed and privileged info contract","https://github.com/danijar/crafter/blob/e04542a2159f1aad3d4c5ad52e8185717380ee3a/crafter/env.py","Achievement-based evaluation","https://github.com/danijar/crafter#evaluation","Observation, actions and recorder","https://github.com/danijar/crafter#interface",[1593],{"_42":240,"_24":1594},"https://github.com/danijar/crafter/blob/main/LICENSE","Repository material under its MIT notice; track any replacement art separately.",[1597],{"_42":1598,"_24":1599,"_259":1600},"Free package and playable GUI","https://github.com/danijar/crafter#play-yourself","pip install crafter pygame; the GUI and evaluation environment run locally.",[1602],{"_42":261,"_24":1603},"https://github.com/danijar/crafter","Python · Gym interface · pixel survival",[824],[141,108],[143,110],[836],{"_42":1598,"_24":1599,"_259":1600},[1613,1614,1615,1616],[1575,1576,1577],[1571,